   278	
   279	He had read himself here twice. It had been night, and he had lain between the embers and this iron with nothing left in him to be frightened with. He had gone to the crowded place under his breastbone and found it where it had always been, with ten things going round it by a way that was worn smooth; and a few old words in pencil had gone onto it, and fitted. He had read it again before light, and told a healer, with his hand on her wrist.
   280	
   281	She had said to write it down and stop touching it.
   282	
   283	He had two findings of that place now. One was hers. It had cost her forty minutes and the floor of herself, at a mill, and it said that there was no flow. The other lay behind his eyes in two words. He had not gone for those, and the tool that gave them had come from a man who said that it was not for men. They did not agree, and he had told nobody.
   284	
   285	The twelfth leaned.
   286	
   287	It had found the iron behind his shoulder: a made thing, driven by a mallet some six cold terms ago. He felt it come about to that, mildly, and he gave his eyes the reeds. There were a great many. He counted the green ones along a yard of the edge until the lean came up short and lay down again.
   288	
   289	Out in the water, a long way off, something knocked twice against stone.
   290	
   291	Lira's head came up at the fire. So did Brom's.
   292	
   293	"It's alive," she said.
   294	
   295	"We left it so," said Cael.
   296	
   297	He took the book out, and wrote by the last of the light.
   298	
   299	*Three hundredth day. The track's end, outside the stone, at the hall's marsh. A hundred and twenty-three: four at a gate, for two skins, meal, a cheese, and corn. Vastin: twenty-one.*
   300	
   301	*The cairn at noon. Her road went north there. She looked up it once, and walked on east. Brom's shoulder has until the three hundred and fifth; that is hers to count, and she has counted it. I did not ask.*
   302	
   303	*Known: the keeper had our skins filled before we came. A man on a bay told him two days ago that a crew would want them.*
   304	
   305	*I am sitting where I read it twice. I have not touched it.*
   306	
   307	*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*

