    20	
    21	On the other side of that yard a stick was grounded already.
    22	
    23	The old man sat with his bound leg out before him, on a folded blanket, and the ash stood upright at his right hand with its foot in a crack. He had been sitting so for an hour. He watched a second stick come across the shale toward him, and a boot after it, and a board; and Cael, who was looking, saw him consider the ground between.
    24	
    25	It sloped a little, there, toward the lip.
    26	
    27	Vastin put out his hand, and lifted the foot of his own stick from its crack, and set it down again a hand's breadth to the left. It made room, on the level part, for another. He did not look up while he did it.
    28	
    29	"I am informed that the ground falls away on that side," he said, to the fire.
    30	
