    36	
    37	Neither of them said another word.
    38	
    39	Lira had her hand over her mouth. Brom was looking very hard into his bowl. On the far side of the fire Teague's boy had opened his own mouth, and the tall man's big chapped hand, which was nearest, came down flat upon his knee and stayed there until he had shut it.
    40	
    41	"Shin," said Oryn.
    42	
    43	She had come round the fire behind the two rows, with her sleeves pushed up, and she stood at her stride and a half from the board.
    44	
    45	"I want my hands in that once before you sleep on it. May I?"
    46	
    47	"Aye," said the broad man again. It appeared that, having found the word, he meant to get the use of it.
    48	
    49	The old woman was there before the healer had knelt.
