    58	
    59	The old woman let the turns close, and smoothed them once with her thumb.
    60	
    61	A man had sat down on the shale at Cael's left while he watched. He had done it as he did it always, in one piece, with his forearms on his knees; but one of the forearms was in linen to the shoulder, and lay along a slat, and he had had to manage it with the other like a thing that he had been given to hold.
    62	
