   273	There was a lamp burning round the corner of the rock.
   274	
   275	He had seen it for an hour, a thread of yellow along the shale, and had left it alone; he knew what she was doing there, and that she would not thank him for a shadow across it. But the thread had not moved for some time. He shut the book, and got up, and went round.
