   142	
   143	"A thousand and eleven," she said. "And a half. It is fifty lengths across, and eleven strides or twelve."
   144	
   145	"Fifty cords," said Brom. "About."
   146	
   147	"About fifty. Something over eleven hundred yards; I make it eleven hundred and seven, as near as hemp will say." She looked at the slip of ash, with its eight nail-marks all in the one place. "And it is round. I have measured a millstone that was not so round. I do not know what was used to cut it."
   148	
   149	It was sharp, and it was perfect; and it had lain out here under that sky with nobody to look at it.
   150	
   151	"And the half of it?" said Cael.
   152	
   153	Karis looked at him. Then she did that sum also, since he had asked.
   154	
   155	"Five hundred and six strides," she said. "From the cut to the middle. You will not see the middle when you come to it. There is nothing there."
   156	
