   214	
   215	She wrote three words under the ring, small. He read them upside down, as he had once read everything.
   216	
   217	*No sixth found.*
   218	
   219	He took out his own book, and wrote the day's entry standing, since he could not well sit, and since he did not care to sit down in front of that floor.
   220	
   221	*Three hundred and seventh day. The fifth place, at the end of the line. A hundred and twenty-three. Vastin: twenty-eight; he was the mark that the round closed on. Oryn is seven days past her cairn. Eleven of us.*
   222	
   223	*A floor of the grey, bare, lying low. Eleven stumps. A cut for an edge. A hundred and fifty-eight lengths and nineteen strides round, by Karis's cord, in three people's hands that were not mine; about fifty lengths across. Round to a nail's breadth. Five hundred and six strides to the middle.*
   224	
   225	*Both edges laid on the line by Karis. They agree. No sixth found.*
   226	
   227	*Nobody has crossed. Deployment since the Line: thirty-four.*
