   282	
   283	"What'd do that?" said Lira.
   284	
   285	"The same as did the plain. Weather." He took his hand away. "I've priced a good many things. I can't price that. I've not got a figure with enough on the end of it."
   286	
   287	He stepped back over, and a healer let go of his wrist.
   288	
   289	Karis went over with her notebook shut. She stood a stride inside, with the rows running away from her feet on either hand; and for the first time that day she let herself look along them.
   290	
   291	"It's the first one."
   292	
   293	Then she came out, and wiped her eyes with the back of her bound hand, and was not ashamed of it.
   294	
   295	Seln was last of the four. He went a stride in, and stood, and came a stride back, with a healer's fingers on him the whole way.
   296	
