   298	
   299	---
   300	
   301	The old man had got up from his box.
   302	
   303	Nobody had bidden him. He came to the cut on the ash, at his own beat, and he did not hold out his wrist to anybody. He stopped with the stick's foot a finger short of the line, and looked down at it.
   304	
   305	It was a sunk stroke in a grey floor, two fingers wide, and he looked at it as Cael had seen him look at a seal.
   306	
   307	"I stood at a line for forty years," Vastin said, "and told people which side of it they were. I never once asked who drew it."
   308	
   309	He lifted his eyes from the cut, and looked along it to the left hand, and to the right, for as far as it could be seen.
   310	
   311	"This is where they drew it."
   312	
   313	He set the ash over the cut, and the bound leg after it.
   314	
   315	Cael watched his eyes go to the air beside his own face, as they had gone on a hillside by a fence, and stay there for a breath. Then he brought the leg back across, and stood on the worn rock with both hands on the stick, and said nothing more to anybody. It was the second time in his life.
   316	
   317	The healer had let the others go by under her fingers, and she did not ask for a wrist now.
   318	
   319	She went to the cut by herself, and stood on the near side of it, with her boots together, like a person at the edge of a pond. She put both her arms out in front of her, at the height of her waist, so that her two hands were over the line and the rest of her was not; and she turned the palms down.
   320	
   321	Cael had seen her stand so once before, at a stone on the Fallow, in the last of the light, and he had not asked her then what she was about.
   322	
   323	She kept them there while a person might have counted fifty. Then she stepped over, one stride, and stood; and stepped back.
   324	
   325	"Nothing," Oryn said. "Everything, round it."
   326	
   327	She had said that to the floor. She turned her head, and said the rest to him.
   328	
   329	"Same as you."
   330	
   331	Nobody answered her.
