   360	
   361	So there were six at the rim, and a healer with a mule.
   362	
   363	The plain had gone dark from edge to edge, and the floor had not. It lay under the first stars as it had lain under the sun, pale and level, with eleven small stumps along its rim; and it seemed to Cael that there was more light in it now than there was in the sky.
   364	
   365	Lira had come to his shoulder.
   366	
