# Coordinator-selected subset of plan-audit.md exact fixes (applied mechanically, 2026-10-12).
# ACCEPTED (14): the ten marker restorations (8-13, 15, 18, 26, 36), minimal, with the source's speakers; Lira's false memory of the plank (14); Karis's souvenir bar (17); the two "five years" (29, 34 -> "for years"; OWNER #18, BOOK_MAP §12 C2).
# AMENDED: 13 (the first line is called by one of the watch — the author's choice which; "in the middle" is the source's staging); 18 (no "called").
# DECLINED:
#  2-7, 16, 23, 24, 37-41 (the read at the seep removed; deployment forced back to thirty-two). No plan text fixes a deployment figure for Movements 8-9; thirty-two was the ENTRY state. The read is the author's staging inside the plan's set piece (Teague's reading still leads: the hour, the old cow, the way in), it is asked for and priced aloud, Pressure is refused, the eyes pay, and Brom's hands do the work. Deployment since the Line stands at THIRTY-THREE from the 302nd.
#  1 (Seln's "There is one to a year."). The six taped rows ARE six yearly sheets (closed Movements 2-3; Karis says so on this same page). Movement 7's ruling limits what the long series proves, not these six.
#  19 (the gloss after the log cut). The protected log says "Tomorrow" and the office's distance is three days; the author's three sentences acknowledge that in Cael's own voice without touching the unit. A reader who can count is better served with it.
#  20 (asterisks nested inside the italic log). The author's typography is right: a word stressed inside italics is set roman; BOOK_MAP §10 says italics are not wording, and nested asterisks would break the italic span.
#  21-22, 27-28 (the year mechanism replaced by flat lines). The protected close itself says "documented four hundred years back - as old as the record"; something on the page must earn that. The mechanism stands; the AUTHOR trims its display (see brief).
#  25 (a sentence telling Oryn of the thirteenth). No plan text requires it in this movement; she refused the count at the fence, and Movement 9's rib reading ("That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now.") is where she meets it. Not told as of the 305th.
#  30-33, 35 (Karis's night stripped of the two pages). The plan's own cutaway is "She holds the refusal in her own head, knows the six-word sentence exists, and does not write it": the refusal cannot be shown without the two things refused. Nothing in the scene states or paraphrases the six words, quotes the leaf, or lays one page on the other; "Second page: nothing entered" continues her closed Movement 6 discipline. It stands.
