editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-A-REPORT.md-246-2. **Two hunks next to logs.** ch21:231 ("and he found that it had been easier to say" → "and it had been easier to say") is in the paragraph that leads into the protected ch21 log; ch4:261 ("a quiet man" → "Seln") is in the paragraph after a log line. Both are narration and both are outside the units. Say if either should go back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-A-REPORT.md-247-3. **Names and the skeleton probe.** Putting a name where an epithet stood moves a sentence toward the source's vocabulary. Two such edits crossed the probe's 0.35 line and I undid them (ch18:117, ch22:211). Smaller upward moves remain inside sentences that do not change class (largest: ch28:283 0.15 → 0.24; ch10:201 0.22 → 0.28; ch15:197 0.40 → 0.45, already close before). No chapter count rose. Lane B is making twice as many name substitutions; `laneA/close_pairs.py` gives the before/after ratio for every changed sentence without printing source text, if you want the same test run there.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-A-REPORT.md-248-4. **ch30:67** ("He found that he saw it again." → "He saw it again.") is inside Seln's cutaway. The brief keeps the cutaways' epithets; I read that as not covering this construction. Revert if you read it otherwise.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-A-REPORT.md:249:5. **ch23:309.** "Seln spoke as he would have priced a wall." became "Seln spoke to the lantern." It is the only edit that puts in words that were not there. He speaks to an object at ch17:125, ch19:77 and ch23:241, and the lantern hangs in that loft (ch23:239), but it is a new small staging detail. If that is too much under "no new material", the plain alternative is to restore the original.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-A-REPORT.md-250-6. **ch30 still has seven "old man"** (nine before). It is the densest cluster in the lane and I had no room left for it inside 25.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-A-REPORT.md:251:7. **ch4:261.** I confirmed against the Book 7 edition (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md:359`, "Seln's keeping the ledger") that the "quiet man" who gave Karis the surveyor's book is Seln. No name was supplied for any unnamed role.
