editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-B-REPORT.md-230-4. **By reading**, the places the brief names: nothing changed inside the eleventh unit (33:155), the twelfth and its two lines (35:297–309), Cleon's warning and the chapter close (35:239–247, 357), the leaf, the account and the chronicle (38:109–215), the fire and pole two (ch40 up to the tail), the grade and Millrace (45:45–189, 271, 305–309, 351–357; 46:151–159, 189, 227, 237), the Span (49:167–169; 50:133, 181–183, 253–259, 315; 51:21–27), the lamps finding and both slips (52:171–251), the close of ch53 (273–305), the pass (54:199–201; ch55 whole), the S22 log (57:253), the court (58:299–381), the centre (ch59 whole), the ledger, the letter, the departures and the closing prose (60:13–35, 69, 149–157, 217–229, 287–303). The roll of twelve at the ford (46:307) and the roll of six (60:289) are untouched.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-B-REPORT.md-231-5. **Perimeters.** No edit tells anybody anything: every change is narration, and none adds a fact. *Still* / *set* / *bones* stand where they stood; Vastin and Teague are untold; Oryn has not heard the leaf; the young one is unnamed. No use of "four hundred", "Architect" or "un-bound" was added; "the court" is lowercase; no season, month or weekday word, and no new name, entered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-B-REPORT.md-232-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-B-REPORT.md:233:**Budget rebalancing (why ten edits were restored).** By chapter 45 I had spent 40 of Priority 1 and 15 of Priority 3. Rather than leave ch46–60 with their epithets and measures while ch31–45 were thinned, I restored the weakest early swaps and spread the numbers: six "old man" (32:297, 34:97, 37:157, 41:165, 42:257, 43:103) and four measures (39:173 finger, 42:61 finger, 44:297 hair, 47:73 thumbs). All ten read exactly as in `pre-lanes/`.
