editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-B-REPORT.md:249:3. **"the old man" for Hesk and for Vastin in ch60.** Scene 2 calls Hesk "the old man" five times (60:5, 59, 61, 67, 71); fifty lines on, "the old man" is Vastin (60:121). By ear the two can blur. I left it, since three of the five sit against the letter. A one-word fix would be "Hesk" at 60:71.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-B-REPORT.md:250:4. **The twin sentence** "He had not lied to the man by the width of a hair." stood at 33:213 and 35:335. I kept the first (it sits against the protected exchange) and trimmed the second to "He had not lied to the man." If the repeat was a deliberate refrain of the debt, restore 35:335.
