editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-17-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-18-### Calendar, running counts, season and units — holds
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-19-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:20:The day spine is intact. The book opens later on Book 7's day 131, after the hearth scene and letter (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:219–265`; `manuscript/chapter-01.md:7`), moves through the cold-term markers at 133, 138, 161, 168, 176, 181 and 263 (`chapter-01.md:199–281`; `chapter-02.md:3`; `chapter-04.md:77–281`; `chapter-05.md:155–267`), reaches Thornwater on 265–268 and the first boat on 277 (`chapter-06.md:3–221`; `chapter-09.md:3–265`), then holds every mapped day through dawn 308. The crucial later spine is explicit: handover 277 (`chapter-12.md:173,299`), cut 279 (`chapter-16.md:191`), spring/fork 280 and Oryn north 281 (`chapter-16.md:221–249`; `chapter-19.md:197`), Treswick 282–294 (`chapter-22.md:3`; `chapter-33.md:283`; `chapter-36.md:15,375`; `chapter-38.md:5`; `chapter-41.md:5,257`), east road 295–297 (`chapter-42.md:9,285`; `chapter-43.md:5,195,203`; `chapter-44.md:217`), Millrace 298 (`chapter-45.md:5,223`; `chapter-46.md:275`), the leg 299–303 (`chapter-46.md:301`; `chapter-47.md:187`; `chapter-48.md:99,327`; `chapter-49.md:259`), Span 304 (`chapter-51.md:341`), shale 305 (`chapter-53.md:261`), pass 306 (`chapter-57.md:245`), court 307 (`chapter-58.md:221`; `chapter-60.md:3–9`) and departures on 308 (`chapter-60.md:103–183`). The cairn is noon on 300 (`chapter-47.md:201–227`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-21-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:22:The subsidiary counts agree. Vastin's month begins on 280 after the 279 injury (`chapter-16.md:191,221–249`); the eleventh day is 290 (`chapter-33.md:145`), the twenty-seventh is 306 (`chapter-54.md:125–175`), the twenty-eighth is 307 (`chapter-58.md:221`) and the twenty-ninth is dawn 308 (`chapter-60.md:183–205`). Lira is twenty-seven days out of wool on 292, twenty-nine on 294 and thirty on 295 (`chapter-37.md:283`; `chapter-41.md:251`; `chapter-42.md:169,285`). Oryn is one day past her cairn on 301, then three/four/five/six/seven/eight on 303–308 (`chapter-48.md:99`; `chapter-49.md:259`; `chapter-51.md:341`; `chapter-53.md:261`; `chapter-57.md:43,245`; `chapter-58.md:221`; `chapter-60.md:183`). Karis receives seven stitches on 290 and has them drawn on 298 (`chapter-33.md:109–113,283`; `chapter-45.md:361–377`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-23-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:24:There are no English weekday names, named months or metric units. Every use of *spring* is the water source or its scene, not a season; *thaw*, *first snow* and *cold term* are event labels. Distances remain feet, yards, miles, paces, strides, furlongs and cords. Cael is nineteen (`chapter-39.md:59`; `chapter-60.md:13`), has no birthday, and the narration gives neither a numbered post-Kindling year count nor a numeric academy-era span.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-25-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-26-### Fragments and deployments — holds
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-27-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:28:The entry ledger is ten fragments and twenty-seven deployments (`chapter-01.md:49,293`). The winter trials are expressly uncounted (`chapter-01.md:285`; `chapter-03.md:293`). The fence, ice-road rescue and ferry read advance the count to 28, 29 and 30 (`chapter-02.md:229‒305`; `chapter-04.md:239–243`; `chapter-09.md:265`). The cut uses Ember and Wind and closes at 32 (`chapter-16.md:191–215`). It stays there through Treswick and Millrace (`chapter-28.md:287`; `chapter-36.md:15,375–379`; `chapter-46.md:287`). The seep is 33 (`chapter-48.md:327`), the second frame at the pass is 34 and the court-floor reading is 35 (`chapter-57.md:249–257`; `chapter-60.md:23`). Five tenth-fragment self-readings and the deliberate twelfth-fragment self-reading are explicitly uncounted (`chapter-21.md:243`; `chapter-57.md:257`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-29-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:30:The eleventh arrives from Vastin's wall in the alley on 290, with *This far?*, rooted plane and no deployment (`chapter-33.md:145–155,293,307`). The twelfth arrives from Cleon's craft on 291, reads made structure rather than meaning, speaks only its single structural words, and charges the eyes (`chapter-35.md:67–139,297`; `chapter-37.md:111`; `chapter-46.md:149–165`; `chapter-47.md:285–307`; `chapter-51.md:345–355`; `chapter-57.md:181–257`). The thirteenth arrives from Teague at the Span, runs through a braced body's length and sends the cost back along its line (`chapter-50.md:119–133`); the shale lining is a trial, not a use (`chapter-53.md:139–149,269`), and its only release is at the pass frame, at nobody (`chapter-55.md:173–253`; `chapter-57.md:249`). Shadow is inventoried as sealed and twice used, with no attribution (`chapter-37.md:223`). No one opens anything of Cael's inside a line beyond the closed text.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-31-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-32-### Money and work ledger — holds
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-33-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:34:The purse sequence is exact: 96 at entry (`chapter-01.md:49`); 76 after the cold stay (`chapter-01.md:243–281`); 116 after the fence (`chapter-02.md:267–295`); 118 after the roof arithmetic (`chapter-06.md:215–225`); 138 after the cut (`chapter-16.md:103,191`); 136 at Treswick entry (`chapter-22.md:199`); 134 after lodging (`chapter-31.md:261–263`; `chapter-33.md:283`); 130 after the archive dinner (`chapter-37.md:139–143,217`); 128 when the rope debt is paid (`chapter-42.md:19–23,285`); 127 at Millrace (`chapter-45.md:299`; `chapter-46.md:275`); 123 on the leg (`chapter-47.md:227–239,299`); and 123 at the end (`chapter-60.md:9,25`). The reserve remains sealed and excluded; personal coppers stay separate (`chapter-01.md:271–281`; `chapter-09.md:281–287`; `chapter-42.md:9–23`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-35-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-36-Pike's book also holds: eleven cloth lines at entry, the clearance as twelfth and Treswick as thirteenth, with the season price blank and later dated but still without a figure (`chapter-01.md:221–281`; `chapter-07.md:199–213`; `chapter-44.md:135–151,217`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-37-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-38-### Bodies — holds
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-39-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:40:Lira's left arm moves from wool to a full month of slow work and is finally named simply as an arm (`chapter-06.md:81–143`; `chapter-37.md:283`; `chapter-42.md:169,285`). Brom's shoulders retain their separate histories, are retied at Millrace, then the pass adds two bolt colours and a left-forearm bolt (`chapter-29.md:3–49`; `chapter-45.md:317–343`; `chapter-50.md:79–107`; `chapter-55.md:3–33`). Karis's left palm has seven Brom stitches, is guarded through the archive, drawn at Millrace, and remains under `Write. Don't lean.` (`chapter-33.md:99–115`; `chapter-38.md:67–73`; `chapter-45.md:361–377`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-41-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:42:Vastin's right knee is closed and bound after the cut, fails under the alley wall, receives a slat and then two fresh laths, and raises the pass wall only sitting under Oryn's amended term (`chapter-16.md:3–67`; `chapter-33.md:3–145`; `chapter-45.md:389–401`; `chapter-54.md:119–175`; `chapter-55.md:35–105`). Teague's Force cost advances wrist, elbow, slat and standing splint warning (`chapter-44.md:267–295`; `chapter-50.md:35–133`; `chapter-51.md:15–27`; `chapter-60.md:131–149`). The broad man's hip, right shin and right shoulder, Cael's collar-bone/ribs/eyes, and Oryn's depletion and first death remain distinct and carried forward (`chapter-50.md:309–357`; `chapter-51.md:3–15,181–195`; `chapter-55.md:131–153,173–253`; `chapter-56.md:245–305`; `chapter-57.md:3–99`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-43-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-44-### Distances and geography — holds
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-45-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-46-The outward and return Lowmarch road agrees: fold, cut, spring, fork-stone, rise and Treswick's five-pier bridge (`chapter-13.md:3–261`; `chapter-16.md:221–249`; `chapter-19.md:197–285`; `chapter-22.md:3–53`; `chapter-37.md:3–131`; `chapter-42.md:3–285`; `chapter-43.md:3–203`). Treswick's three walls, four-alley lane, carts' street, yard door, twenty-seven-step stair, galleries and twenty-two-step cut remain mutually legible (`chapter-22.md:53–199`; `chapter-23.md:149–281`; `chapter-26.md:3–277`; `chapter-27.md:3–91`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-47-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:48:Lowmarch–Millrace and the eastward leg keep their mapped order: Stair rim, noon cairn, Hall marsh, dead hold, chock-stones, seep, crest (`chapter-44.md:229–321`; `chapter-45.md:223–401`; `chapter-47.md:3–307`; `chapter-48.md:3–327`). At the Span the shelf, ravine, gap, arch and 440 yards plus two strides to the middle agree (`chapter-49.md:139–195`; `chapter-51.md:181–227`). The shale steps lead to the notch/pass and then the court. The court measures approximately fifty cords or 1,107 yards across and 506 strides to centre (`chapter-52.md:27–43`; `chapter-54.md:303–331`; `chapter-58.md:103–147`; `chapter-59.md:1–105`). The five sites can lie on the single bearing with their corner figures increasing eastward and the unfigured fifth oldest-last (`chapter-45.md:81–173`; `chapter-52.md:77–129`; `chapter-58.md:153–227`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-49-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-50-### Quotations, names and seams — hold
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-51-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:52:Quoted returns do not drift. Oryn's `Write it down and stop touching it.` recurs exactly (`chapter-20.md:97`; `chapter-35.md:107`). `It's six people's.` is first Lira's limit, then Cael's answer, then Vastin's remembered refusal (`chapter-35.md:165`; `chapter-42.md:157`; `chapter-59.md:317`). `If there's road` passes from Lira to Cael unchanged (`chapter-46.md:269`; `chapter-59.md:225`). `Mind the stair. It leans.` appears once (`chapter-41.md:205`). The cord-on-stone image is not falsely promoted into a quotation (`chapter-20.md:197`). Cleon's full warning occurs once (`chapter-35.md:239–247`); the protected log's `Cleon said don't` is shorthand, not a second statement of its content (`chapter-57.md:253`). Pole one remains the cord/stone finding; pole two is Lira's existence sentence and Cael's built-no-room sentence (`chapter-20.md:189–207`; `chapter-40.md:19,185–205`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-53-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:54:`Noted` remains speaker-accurate: Cael to Vastin and Teague (`chapter-43.md:91–95`; `chapter-48.md:89–97`; `chapter-60.md:149–157,215–221`), Vastin twice at Millrace (`chapter-45.md:169–175,397–405`), Teague twice (`chapter-49.md:167–169`; `chapter-51.md:21–27`) and the young one once (`chapter-54.md:199–203`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-55-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:56:No planned anonymous role is newly named. The young one's name is conveyed only by its effect (`chapter-55.md:149–153`); the tall spear-carrier is a man (`chapter-54.md:203`; `chapter-60.md:161`); the other three, the watch, clerks, keepers, factors, carters and the net-woman remain unnamed. *The Sunken Span* is explicitly a carters' name (`chapter-49.md:3–11`). Book 7's hearth ending flows directly into the same-morning Book 8 river walk, and chapter 60 reaches the mapped west/north/west-separately ending without inventing a Book 9 seam (`chapter-01.md:3–49`; `chapter-60.md:103–303`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-57-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-58-## 2. The record's limits
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-59-
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-66-- Cleon authenticates one hand, age and fair construction but expressly not truth (`chapter-40.md:95–105`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-67-- Vastin reduces his history to *aimed*, category and person (`chapter-40.md:121–129`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-68-- Cael's pole two is `built ... no room` / `so that I wouldn't happen` (`chapter-40.md:183–189`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:69:- The 298th log dates the already-drawn line; the 305th close compares record, Architect and machine ages (`chapter-45.md:227`; `chapter-53.md:287`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:70:- Vastin starts the apparatus→sigils inference on the blanket and is stopped; at the court he starts the old man/apparatus sentence and stops himself (`chapter-52.md:179–195`; `chapter-59.md:325`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:71:- The protected closing prose supplies the final book-level restatement (`chapter-60.md:303`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-72-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-73-These are interpretations or mapped summaries, not quotations. Karis's one account remains the only record-voice paraphrase (`chapter-38.md:137–163`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-74-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:75:`Four hundred years` occurs exactly five times, all allowed: Karis's account (`chapter-38.md:155`), Cael's pole two (`chapter-40.md:185`), the 298th log (`chapter-45.md:227`), the 305th close (`chapter-53.md:287`) and protected closing prose (`chapter-60.md:303`). `The Architect` occurs three times: Vastin's copied reference (`chapter-12.md:65`), Karis's title definition (`chapter-38.md:147–155`) and the 305th historical comparison (`chapter-53.md:287`). It is never a present actor.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-76-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-77-The chronicle line is spoken once and its hole remains physical and unglossed (`chapter-38.md:185–215`). `[UNBOUND]` at `chapter-27.md:181` is a stratum boundary; six later *un-bound* occurrences belong to the record, Karis's account and her copy (`chapter-38.md:109,119,159,259`). The record reports fear of that historical kind; the narration does not endorse it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-78-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:79:The two pages remain unjoined. The closest approach deliberately occupies opposite ends of Brom's blanket and is stopped before inference (`chapter-52.md:153–195`). No dialogue, narration or cutaway connects the leaf to lamps, sigils, Arbiters, plates or stations as a finding. Vastin's sentence stops in the chamber, at the blanket and again in his own court-night interior (`chapter-38.md:219–239`; `chapter-52.md:177–195`; `chapter-59.md:325`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-80-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-81-`terminal` and `infrastructure` occur zero times. **Finding:** `circuit` occurs once at `chapter-23.md:149`, in the ordinary phrase `whole circuit of the bluff`; the zero rule is lexical, so it still needs replacement.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-82-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:83:The deep-layer date is read separately by Cael and Seln, never printed, spoken, written or arithmetically worked on the page (`chapter-18.md:3–93`; `chapter-42.md:267–271`; `chapter-52.md:203–211`). Made objects receive no mind, will or intention; the Arbiter never speaks. The protected `did not *notice*` line is the mapped Cael-language exception, not narrator endorsement (`chapter-58.md:343–361`). Outside the protected close, no line states or completes the third sentence. *Recurrence*, *primordial*, *source* as identity, *tomb* and capitalized *Court* do not appear.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-84-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-85-## 3. Knowledge perimeters and unpaid debts
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-86-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-87-The perimeters hold.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-88-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-89-- **Mechanism:** the six know it. Cleon learns how the twelfth alone arrived (`chapter-35.md:203–247`); nobody extends that to the other fragments.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:90:- **Eleventh:** Cael and Lira know; Oryn learns at Millrace; Vastin is never told that it is his (`chapter-33.md:149–155,293`; `chapter-46.md:35–45`; `chapter-60.md:29`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:91:- **Twelfth:** Lira is first, then the other four and Cleon; Oryn learns at Millrace (`chapter-35.md:139–247`; `chapter-36.md:27`; `chapter-46.md:35–45`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:92:- **Thirteenth:** Lira and Brom learn first, Oryn learns after the pass use, and Teague never learns (`chapter-51.md:49–63`; `chapter-53.md:133–149`; `chapter-56.md:279–295`; `chapter-57.md:249`; `chapter-60.md:29`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:93:- **Private inward findings:** *still*, *set* and the deliberate inward reading are told to no one. Lira identifies the eye cost but receives no words at Millrace; at the shale camp she pushes the log back unread (`chapter-46.md:247–269`; `chapter-57.md:181–257,283–297`). The protected log phrase `Cleon said don't` does not reproduce his warning; its substance remains Cael/Cleon only.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:94:- **Leaf and grade:** Karis, Cleon, Cael and Vastin hear the leaf; Lira, Brom and Seln read the copy; Oryn and Teague never do (`chapter-38.md:95–125`; `chapter-40.md:3–91`; `chapter-60.md:211–229`). The grade/ages are known at the Millrace table; Teague receives the operational oldest-last result, not the record (`chapter-45.md:81–217`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:95:- **Others:** Teague's four learn wall doctrine and field terms, not mechanism or fragments (`chapter-44.md:169–213,267–315`; `chapter-54.md:181–203`). The watch and faction see effects but receive no identities or explanation (`chapter-32.md:55–151`; `chapter-50.md:101–313`). Teague infers only that Vastin was somebody; he does not learn the former office (`chapter-44.md:13–35`). The two seals and Seln's case contents remain unnamed (`chapter-52.md:235–273`; `chapter-49.md:211–213`; `chapter-60.md:57–61`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-96-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:97:The unpaid acquisition debts remain live and legible. Cael cannot tell Vastin or Teague without disclosing a mechanism that belongs to six; using the thirteenth to save Teague does not pay a debt the creditor cannot know (`chapter-42.md:147–157`; `chapter-53.md:133–149`; `chapter-60.md:25–33`). Vastin remains sixth only by Seln's count, unadmitted, and neither asks nor is asked (`chapter-59.md:309–333`; `chapter-60.md:275–299`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-98-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-99-## 4. Consent and the Reader Standard
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-100-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:101:The consent covenant holds. Every ordinary healer reading is asked and answered: Lira and Vastin at Thornwater/cut (`chapter-06.md:81–161`; `chapter-19.md:119–173`), the bodies at Millrace (`chapter-45.md:317–401`), Oryn's deep read (`chapter-46.md:75–89`), the Span injuries (`chapter-50.md:343–357`; `chapter-51.md:185–195`), Vastin's amended wall term (`chapter-54.md:137–175`), Cael's ribs (`chapter-56.md:253–305`) and the post-centre read (`chapter-59.md:197–215`). The one impossible case is faced honestly: Oryn asks the young one, waits one breath for an answer that cannot come, then performs the emergency check and later distinguishes necessity from leave (`chapter-55.md:131–145`; `chapter-57.md:3–99`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-102-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:103:The death is brief, non-graphic, prepared by the young one's established half-beat and responsibility, and not used as a shortcut to Cael's centre revelation (`chapter-48.md:273–327`; `chapter-53.md:3–31`; `chapter-54.md:197–203`; `chapter-55.md:107–153`). Burial, eleven bowls, Teague's missing count, the hot cloth and Oryn's first-death accounting carry the cost (`chapter-56.md:3–59,181–229`; `chapter-57.md:3–99`). Retreating opponents are not struck at the cut, Span or pass (`chapter-15.md:231–275`; `chapter-50.md:287–313`; `chapter-55.md:275–311`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-104-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:105:A thirteen-year-old will understand what Cael owes and why he cannot yet pay: the book states both debts, the shared ownership of the mechanism and the difference between rescue and disclosure in plain terms (`chapter-42.md:147–157`; `chapter-60.md:25–33`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-106-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-107-## 5. Book-wide repetition — the worst ten
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-108-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-109-Counts are case-insensitive lexical/formula counts over all sixty manuscript files. Some are deliberate motif counts, not sixty separate defects; the issue is cumulative audibility.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-110-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:111:1. **Counting language — 518.** `count/counted/counting/counts` is the book's governing mind, but by the archive it becomes the default transition, observation and emotional defence (`chapter-01.md:17`; `chapter-27.md:285`; `chapter-59.md:1`). Preserve actual ledgers and tactical counts; reduce reflexive count narration where no figure changes.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:112:2. **Role epithets — 377.** `old man` 239, `small pale woman` 60, `big man` 60, `quiet man` 18. They protect point of view and anonymity early, but named intimates still receive the labels late (`chapter-38.md:135`; `chapter-44.md:7–23`; `chapter-60.md:289`). The closing six-person epithet roll is the clearest overreach.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:113:3. **`flat` — 275.** This includes the courier's *flat*, flat hands, flat ground and flat delivery (`chapter-17.md:3–43`; `chapter-44.md:311–315`; `chapter-52.md:27–43`). The noun is canonically necessary; the gesture/adverb uses need thinning.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:114:4. **`as a/an man/person/woman/boy/girl ...` — 176.** These explanatory comparisons often restate an already visible action (`chapter-15.md:25`; `chapter-44.md:315`; `chapter-52.md:29`). They are the most audible sentence-level mannerism.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:115:5. **Entry language — 134.** `enter/entered/entry/entries` properly belongs to Cael and the offices, but it spreads into ordinary emotional narration (`chapter-21.md:131–163`; `chapter-44.md:145–151`; `chapter-60.md:17–35`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-116-6. **Price/bill language — 96.** Brom's idiom and fragment costs justify much of it; other viewpoints borrow it often enough to blur speaker texture (`chapter-05.md:217`; `chapter-40.md:49–65`; `chapter-44.md:189–213`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:117:7. **`did not/didn't look` — 90.** Looking away is a real covenant, but the same negative gesture serves fear, courtesy, privacy, tactical discipline and grief (`chapter-15.md:173`; `chapter-31.md:71`; `chapter-60.md:241`). Keep deliberate Cleon/Cael look-away beats; vary routine blocking.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:118:8. **`nobody said/spoke/answered` — 52.** Silence repeatedly receives its own explanatory tag after the scene has already made it audible (`chapter-05.md:109`; `chapter-40.md:23`; `chapter-54.md:249`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:119:9. **`He found that` — 48.** The phrase delays direct realization and recurs across viewpoints (`chapter-15.md:197`; `chapter-39.md:47`; `chapter-60.md:97`). Most can simply state the discovery.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-120-10. **`not X ... but Y` — 43.** This heuristic count excludes cross-sentence antitheses; the construction is strongest at genuine epistemic turns and weaker in ordinary qualification (`chapter-39.md:19`; `chapter-40.md:43`; `chapter-44.md:315`). Preserve pole language and research limits; cut routine reversals.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-121-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-122-Secondary tallies confirm the same texture: finger-width expressions 38; `told ... no` 36; `for a moment/while` 31; hands on stick/ash 23; thumbs in belts 19; `squared` 18; `lay down` 13; quarter-turns 0. `He told it no` is especially audible when adjacent to the 518-count/134-entry system (`chapter-34.md:13–15`; `chapter-36.md:343`; `chapter-42.md:295`).
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-125-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-126-### The argument
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-127-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:128:The book builds the planned argument rather than merely announcing it. Pole one turns Cael's still-place problem from a bad measurement into an instrument limit (`chapter-20.md:189–207`; `chapter-21.md:215–243`). The Millrace waypost read makes the twelfth independently say *still/set* without resolving the conflict (`chapter-46.md:135–175`). The leaf and pole two then turn *the system forgot me* into *it was built so there would be no room* (`chapter-38.md:95–163`; `chapter-40.md:19,169–205`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-129-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:130:The grade converts history into direction (`chapter-45.md:81–173`); Millrace splits the two instruments' findings (`chapter-46.md:135–219`); the Span proves the oldest-last road passes through guarded knowledge (`chapter-50.md:101–313`; `chapter-51.md:203–227`); the pass makes a wall's ethical failure cost a life without making the wall morally false (`chapter-55.md:107–165`); and the court/centre converts exclusion into fit while withholding identity (`chapter-58.md:321–361`; `chapter-59.md:111–185`; `chapter-60.md:303`). The third sentence is felt, not owned.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-131-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-132-### Length and local pacing
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-133-
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-137-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-138-- **Movement 5, about 36,000 words:** entry mechanics, Cleon's method and the alley attack make the archive physically and morally costly. Its apparent slowness is part of the claim that knowledge is work (`chapter-27.md:3–289`; `chapter-33.md:3–307`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-139-- **Movement 6, 36,150 words:** twelfth acquisition, warning, dividers, leaf and fire form one continuous turn. The length is earned, though the repeated lamp/hand/looking-away language makes it feel longer than its event count (`chapter-34.md:3–253`; `chapter-40.md:3–289`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:140:- **Movement 8, 37,130 words:** the repeated road is not nostalgia; old places are reread under new ownership, then scarcity, the Span and blanket force the two crews to become operationally real (`chapter-47.md:3–307`; `chapter-53.md:3–291`). It is earned. The mildest sag is the second half of the return road, roughly `chapter-47.md:195–chapter-48.md:105`, where travel confirmation and watcher evidence accumulate before the seep changes the count. Texture compression, not beat removal, is the remedy.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-141-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:142:Nothing important is rushed. The death has burial, blame, a changed count and a full night before the deliberate inward read (`chapter-55.md:107–153`; `chapter-56.md:3–229`; `chapter-57.md:3–181`). The centre gets the entire 306–308 sequence and an after-reading before the departure (`chapter-58.md:3–361`; `chapter-60.md:3–303`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-143-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-144-## 7. Protected lines
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-145-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:146:The leaf, chronicle, technician's sheet, directive/objection, lamps finding, fragment notices, two poles, grade, Pike lines, court lines, departures, S22 log, Hesk letter and closing prose are each printed once where mapped. No protected document is printed twice. The owner-pending defaults stand: the young one's name is not printed (`chapter-55.md:149–153`); `Tell Lira's family I said so.` has no setup (`chapter-60.md:69`); all three #57 Path/machine lines and `the whole year` are exact (`chapter-53.md:287`; `chapter-58.md:343–361`; `chapter-57.md:253`; `chapter-60.md:303`); the spear-carrier is a man (`chapter-54.md:203`; `chapter-60.md:161`); and the date is never printed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-147-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-148-**Three protected-pattern units fail the character-for-character lock:**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-149-
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-151-2. `manuscript/chapter-45.md:303–309`: the locked `Lira said, "Sixth chair."` / `Oryn said, "On my terms. Which are the only kind."` has become `"Sixth chair," she said.` plus an unattributed second line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-152-3. `manuscript/chapter-45.md:351–357`: the locked explicit Oryn attributions around `You listened when it told you the second time.` and `Once is once more than I priced.` are absent, although the spoken wording remains.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-153-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:154:These must be restored from the protected source, not rewritten through the line-fix list below.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-155-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-156-## 8. Reader Standard
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-157-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-158-The book is appropriate for a thirteen-year-old reader. Violence is tense but not lingering; birth and death are handled without graphic detail; institutional harm is concrete; and the record's fear is reported rather than ratified.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-159-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:160:The archive run (`chapter-27.md:3–chapter-41.md:257`) can be followed by ear because every abstraction is attached to a physical object, speaker and refusal. A young reader may not retain custody of every sheet, but will retain the necessary chain: floors are instructions; Cleon reads their lean; Karis recovers language; the leaf says the system was made for a reason. The grade in chapter 45 is the densest single sequence (`chapter-45.md:5–173`). Its intermediate figures may require a reread, but *the marks grade age, ages rise east, oldest-last* is cleanly restated (`chapter-45.md:151–173`). The blanket is similarly dense (`chapter-52.md:41–213`), but its physical layout makes the core prohibition audible: evidence on one side, record on the other, no line between.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-161-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-162-The prose does not read too young. The low computed grade is a vocabulary artifact, not a cognitive measure.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md-163-
