editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-008/plan-audit-apply.md-69-   old: `[[TIER-B: the S20 close — "It's here," Karis said. "Third-tier, documented four hundred years back — as old as the record, as old as the Architect, as old as the machine. The first one they made, or near it." / "And it's on the line." / "It's the *end* of the line. Oldest-last. Everything before it was practice, or maintenance, or — I don't have the word. This is the one that's been quiet since before quiet had a name." … "You still want to stand in the middle of it." / "More than I've wanted anything since I was fourteen." / "Why." / "Because every other site, my Path worked while everyone's died. I want to know what the *oldest* one does to me. I think it's going to tell me something the records can't." — the plan pins only the first speaker (Karis) and carries one elision before "You still want…". Staged: Karis on a stone at the box's lid with her finger beside the thumbnail ring, Cael standing at her shoulder; she has just worked the reduction and says the figure here, once; the alternation runs Karis / Cael / Karis … Karis / Cael / Karis / Cael. Nothing of mine stands between her finger going down and the fixed last line below — coordinator to supply protected text]]`
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-008/plan-audit-apply.md-70-   new: `"It's here," Karis said. "Third-tier, documented four hundred years back — as old as the record, as old as the Architect, as old as the machine. The first one they made, or near it."\n\n"And it's on the line."\n\n"It's the *end* of the line. Oldest-last. Everything before it was practice, or maintenance, or — I don't have the word. This is the one that's been quiet since before quiet had a name."\n\n{{JOIN}}\n\n"You still want to stand in the middle of it."\n\n"More than I've wanted anything since I was fourteen."\n\n"Why."\n\n{{JOIN}}\n\n"Because every other site, my Path worked while everyone's died. I want to know what the *oldest* one does to me. I think it's going to tell me something the records can't."`
--
