editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-009/plan-audit-apply.md-39-   old: `[[TIER-B: the S23 close — "Every other one, yours worked and ours died." / "Yes." / "You think this one's different." / "I think this one's the first one they made," … "I think if any place on the continent is going to tell me what I am, it's the one they built to make sure I'd never be." / He stepped over the line. / His Path did not die. It also did not *notice* it should have. / "Wait here," he said, and did not look back, and walked toward the center of the oldest quiet, alone. — the plan calls this "Lira's fixed exchange" and gives it with one elision, so no speaker is pinned line by line and the break inside the long speech is not shown. Staged here: dusk at the western stump; Lira at Cael's left shoulder, the other four of the six behind them, Oryn by the mule, Teague's three turned away; the first and third lines hers, the second and fourth his; nothing of mine stands between her coming to his shoulder and this unit, and it closes the chapter. OWNER-pending #57's sentence stands inside it as the plan prints it — coordinator to supply protected text]]`
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-009/plan-audit-apply.md-40-   new: `"Every other one, yours worked and ours died," Lira said.\n\n"Yes," Cael said.\n\n"You think this one's different."\n\n"I think this one's the first one they made," he said. "I think if any place on the continent is going to tell me what I am, it's the one they built to make sure I'd never be."\n\nHe stepped over the line.\n\nHis Path did not die. It also did not *notice* it should have.\n\n"Wait here," he said, and did not look back, and walked toward the center of the oldest quiet, alone.`
