editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-009/plan-audit-apply.md-55-   old: `[[TIER-B: Teague's departure — "The thaw's past," / "Noted," / "After the next thaw." … "Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." — Tier A 22 heads the unit "Teague:" but does not say which of the first two lines is his and which the answer, and it elides between "After the next thaw." and "Whatever's on the next line." Staged here: dawn of the 308th at the western side of the fire, Teague a stride from Cael with the letter already in his coat, his three standing behind him; the term that he set at Lowmarch ("After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes.") has been kept, and this is its successor. Nothing of mine stands between his last speech above and this unit; the paragraph below has him go — coordinator to supply protected text]]`
