editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-009/plan-audit-apply.md-59-   old: `She went along them, before she would get up, as she had gone along six people at a fork-stone. She looked under the linen on Brom's forearm, having asked, and told him that he was to keep it out of the wet and that the colours on his chest were coming on nicely. She took Karis's left hand, by her leave, and turned it to the light. She told Lira nothing whatever, since there was nothing that wanted telling, and Lira said that she had noticed.`
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-009/plan-audit-apply.md-60-   new: `She went along them, before she would get up, as she had gone along six people at a fork-stone. She looked under the linen on Brom's forearm, having asked, and told him that he was to keep it out of the wet and that the colours on his chest were coming on nicely. She took Karis's left hand, by her leave, and turned it to the light. "It'll leave a line," she said. She told Lira nothing whatever, since there was nothing that wanted telling, and Lira said that she had noticed.`
