editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-009/plan-audit-apply.md-63-   old: `[[TIER-B: Oryn's departure — "The day I have to." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that." … "They'll carry. They'll hurt," … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." — Tier A 22 heads the unit "Oryn:" and elides twice; the "Noted," between her first and third lines is not pinned. Staged here: dawn of the 308th at the rim, the mule unloaded, three boxes on the rock at Cael's feet; her first line answers his question above about the leaf (she has still not heard it); "Noted," reads as his; "They'll carry. They'll hurt," is said of his ribs with her eyes on the box that he must take up; the last line is her term, as in her letter. If "The day I have to." answers something else, my question above wants turning. The paragraph below has her go — coordinator to supply protected text]]`
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-009/plan-audit-apply.md-64-   new: `"The day I have to," Oryn said.\n\n"Noted," said Cael.\n\n"Everybody says that."\n\n{{JOIN}}\n\n"They'll carry. They'll hurt," Oryn said.\n\n{{JOIN}}\n\n"After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say."`
