+# Book 8 listening proof — Part 4 working notes
+
+Range: `manuscript/chapter-46.md` through `manuscript/chapter-60.md` only. I printed and read all fifteen files in full, in order: 79,365 words and 84 scenes. The boundary words below are transcribed from the manuscript, with Markdown retained where it falls inside the six-word sample.
+
+## Chapter-by-chapter reading record
+
+### Chapter 46 — Not Flow — 6 scenes
+
+#### Scene 1
+
+- First six words: `He found her above the weir,`
+- Last six words: `stone. "But not on my plank."`
+- Oryn's confession and her terms are attributable throughout; the twelve findings remain distinct when heard. Clean.
+
+#### Scene 2
+
+- First six words: `The miller shut the sluice at`
+- Last six words: `more you mean to bring me."`
+- Oryn's questions, Cael's answers, and the miller's interruption all have audible owners. Clean.
+
+#### Scene 3
+
+- First six words: `"Now the middle," said Oryn. It`
