+1. **Chapter 46, line 231.**
+   - Before: `The paper stayed where it was. Cael had put his hand to his coat when the girl began, and he took it away again.`
+   - Join: `He was not sorry. She had drawn a line round her own table; and it was the same line that Karis had drawn on a desk with a bound hand: what a person had found went on one page, and what a person had been told went on another.`
+   - After: `"Go to bed," said Oryn. "The pair of you. I'm going to sit here until I can stand."`
