+   - Vastin clarifier: `Vastin inclined his head, by about the width of a finger.`
+   - Ruling: sound; decline the one-word substitution. Hesk is named twice in the letter scene before the first phrase, while Vastin is named in the next sentence of a separate departure scene. A listener is not asked to carry an unresolved old man across the break.
